# UI responsive (must)

Mobile-first is required on every landing and section.

## Breakpoints

| Label | Width | Expectation |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| Phone SE | ~320px | No horizontal scroll; compact nav; CTAs full-width OK |
| Mobile | ~390px | Primary mobile layout; hamburger |
| Tablet | ~768px | 2-col cards where useful |
| Laptop | ~1024px | Desktop nav (`lg:`) |
| Desktop | ~1280px+ | Full grids |

## Rules

1. Mobile-first Tailwind; enhance with `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` / `xl:`
2. No overflow: `min-w-0`, `max-w-full`, `overflow-x-clip` on shells
3. Long CTAs: `whitespace-normal`, `w-full sm:w-auto`
4. Swiper: touch-friendly, no horizontal page scroll
5. Comfortable touch targets
6. Do not ship desktop-only then shrink

## After UI changes

Verify 320 / 390 / 768 / 1024 / 1280+; fix overflow before done.
